1
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:35,050
[In my prime]

2
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:37,820
[Episode 17]

3
00:01:38,479 --> 00:01:39,039
Sweetie,

4
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:41,310
you finally called me.

5
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:43,200
I knew it.

6
00:01:43,509 --> 00:01:44,910
My hunch is always right.

7
00:01:46,479 --> 00:01:48,210
Did you eat your birthday cake?

8
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:50,650
And the fried mushrooms,

9
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:51,880
the buns and all that—

10
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:53,180
did they get to you?

11
00:01:54,590 --> 00:01:55,070
Dad,

12
00:01:55,479 --> 00:01:56,430
it's my birthday.

13
00:01:56,430 --> 00:01:58,360
I'm not gonna shortchange myself.

14
00:01:58,560 --> 00:02:00,240
I ordered a huge bowl

15
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:01,590
of thick‑cut noodles

16
00:02:01,590 --> 00:02:02,560
with lots of meat in it.

17
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:04,020
See? I'm eating right now.

18
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:07,510
It's very chewy.

19
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,520
Next time you come to Haizhou,

20
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:11,120
I'll bring you here to try it.

21
00:02:11,590 --> 00:02:13,590
Good, as long as you're eating well.

22
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:15,280
Your mom

23
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:17,120
worries about you out there alone,

24
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:18,320
not eating properly.

25
00:02:19,250 --> 00:02:21,000
And about the address.

26
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:23,079
Dad, I moved to a new place.

27
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Yeah, I didn't like

28
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,680
the place I lived in before.

29
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:29,240
You know, I've made some money,

30
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:30,310
so I'm thinking of moving

31
00:02:30,310 --> 00:02:32,120
to a place with a better environment.

32
00:02:32,120 --> 00:02:35,370
Tell uncle to take

33
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:36,640
the buns and mushrooms back.

34
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:37,780
I don't have a fridge

35
00:02:38,910 --> 00:02:41,310
where I live right now,
so I can't keep them.

36
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:43,079
Really?

37
00:02:44,470 --> 00:02:45,030
Okay.

38
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:48,610
Have you settled in yet?

39
00:02:49,470 --> 00:02:51,730
Don't forget to send me your new address.

40
00:02:52,790 --> 00:02:53,910
Living alone in a new city,

41
00:02:53,910 --> 00:02:55,260
you've got to stay safe.

42
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:56,870
Just make sure

43
00:02:56,870 --> 00:02:58,710
I can reach you if something comes up.

44
00:02:58,710 --> 00:03:00,400
I know, Dad. Don't worry.

45
00:03:13,680 --> 00:03:14,190
Ma'am,

46
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:16,120
I didn't order a poached egg.

47
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:17,820
The table over there
ordered it for you just now.

48
00:03:17,820 --> 00:03:18,960
He said it's not easy for a young girl

49
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:20,190
to be away from home,

50
00:03:20,590 --> 00:03:22,390
and wished you a happy birthday.

51
00:04:19,870 --> 00:04:20,680
I'm sorry.

52
00:04:21,269 --> 00:04:22,730
You didn't react just now,

53
00:04:23,040 --> 00:04:25,440
so I got curious
what you were listening to.

54
00:04:26,040 --> 00:04:27,500
Just randomly listening.

55
00:04:28,980 --> 00:04:29,690
[Fundamentals of Mechanical Engineering]

56
00:04:29,730 --> 00:04:31,260
Aren't you a finance major?

57
00:04:29,730 --> 00:04:30,800
[Mechanical Engineering Drawing]

58
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:33,260
Why are you reading these?

59
00:04:45,630 --> 00:04:46,300
Are you okay?

60
00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:46,830
I'm fine.

61
00:04:47,270 --> 00:04:48,570
I was counting my steps

62
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:49,659
and didn't notice.

63
00:04:50,530 --> 00:04:51,360
One of your strides

64
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:52,560
is about two of mine.

65
00:04:52,830 --> 00:04:54,159
I was just testing that.

66
00:04:55,950 --> 00:04:56,360
Okay.

67
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:58,720
I figured someone

68
00:04:58,720 --> 00:04:59,850
as impressive as you

69
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:01,920
would be listening to English
wherever you go,

70
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:03,920
killing it in extracurriculars

71
00:05:04,190 --> 00:05:05,920
like swimming and basketball,

72
00:05:06,070 --> 00:05:07,950
and probably playing an instrument too.

73
00:05:07,950 --> 00:05:09,810
That's not me you're describing.

74
00:05:11,800 --> 00:05:12,660
I noticed.

75
00:05:13,870 --> 00:05:15,000
It really isn't you.

76
00:05:16,070 --> 00:05:16,830
In the library,

77
00:05:16,830 --> 00:05:18,510
you read books from other majors,

78
00:05:18,510 --> 00:05:20,830
and listen to the theme songs
of idol dramas.

79
00:05:20,830 --> 00:05:21,680
Cao Xin,

80
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:24,500
you're very different
from what I imagined.

81
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:26,390
I originally wanted to major

82
00:05:26,390 --> 00:05:27,630
in mechanical engineering,

83
00:05:27,630 --> 00:05:29,270
but my family wouldn't let me.

84
00:05:29,270 --> 00:05:30,390
Well, you could switch majors

85
00:05:30,390 --> 00:05:31,320
for grad school.

86
00:05:32,150 --> 00:05:33,830
I haven't decided if I'll go

87
00:05:34,310 --> 00:05:35,320
to grad school yet.

88
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:35,870
If you make up your mind,

89
00:05:35,870 --> 00:05:36,800
you can come to me.

90
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:37,460
Come to you?

91
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:40,159
I'm planning to study abroad
for my master's.

92
00:05:40,159 --> 00:05:41,100
But

93
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:42,640
I lack self-discipline.

94
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:43,810
I need a study buddy.

95
00:05:47,190 --> 00:05:47,520
Okay.

96
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:49,840
I have class later. Gotta go.

97
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:54,940
Remember to come to me.

98
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:20,420
You really want to work for me?

99
00:06:20,420 --> 00:06:21,830
You're a college student.

100
00:06:21,830 --> 00:06:23,360
You could do anything.

101
00:06:24,040 --> 00:06:25,330
Even just dating.

102
00:06:25,430 --> 00:06:27,040
I'm just working to pay my tuition.

103
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:27,560
You know what

104
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:28,830
my family's situation is.

105
00:06:28,830 --> 00:06:29,600
Besides,

106
00:06:29,940 --> 00:06:31,210
didn't we agree?

107
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:31,740
When you're the boss,

108
00:06:31,740 --> 00:06:32,890
you have to hire me.

109
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:34,480
All right, Zhang.

110
00:06:36,430 --> 00:06:36,970
Even though

111
00:06:36,970 --> 00:06:37,560
I'm also

112
00:06:37,580 --> 00:06:38,730
barely scraping by,

113
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:40,600
since you're with me now,

114
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:42,120
we start with a street stall.

115
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:43,480
Every penny counts.

116
00:06:44,190 --> 00:06:45,370
I won't let you work for nothing.

117
00:06:45,370 --> 00:06:45,750
Okay.

118
00:06:45,830 --> 00:06:46,360
Go ahead.

119
00:06:46,590 --> 00:06:47,650
Hang the lights, open for business.

120
00:06:47,650 --> 00:06:48,159
Okay.

121
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:54,190
-Come check it out!
-Authentic export surplus!

122
00:06:54,190 --> 00:06:54,830
The latest styles!

123
00:06:54,830 --> 00:06:56,900
Factory clearance, export surplus!

124
00:06:57,159 --> 00:06:58,680
Our clothes' quality is unmatched—

125
00:06:58,680 --> 00:06:59,870
all export surplus.

126
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:00,560
Look.

127
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:02,310
Is this really export surplus?

128
00:07:02,310 --> 00:07:02,800
Yes.

129
00:07:03,010 --> 00:07:04,810
Why are the tags still attached?

130
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:08,360
Let me tell you.

131
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:09,830
Here's the thing.

132
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:11,950
These clothes were all custom orders

133
00:07:11,950 --> 00:07:13,190
from foreigners.

134
00:07:13,510 --> 00:07:14,800
We've got serious connections

135
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:16,040
with the factory

136
00:07:16,070 --> 00:07:17,270
to score this batch.

137
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:19,310
Definitely authentic export surplus.

138
00:07:19,310 --> 00:07:20,870
See? Look at this.

139
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:22,250
The tag's cut off.

140
00:07:22,250 --> 00:07:23,120
With this quality,

141
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:25,050
it'll easily last you three years.

142
00:07:26,390 --> 00:07:26,920
Ladies,

143
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:28,760
looking for authentic export surplus?

144
00:07:28,760 --> 00:07:30,040
New store opening!

145
00:07:30,110 --> 00:07:31,910
Ladies, come support us!

146
00:07:32,110 --> 00:07:34,230
Authentic export surplus!
Come take a look!

147
00:07:34,230 --> 00:07:35,000
Ladies,

148
00:07:35,159 --> 00:07:36,240
check out our clothes.

149
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:37,770
Look at this great quality.

150
00:07:37,870 --> 00:07:38,830
Come take a look!

151
00:07:38,830 --> 00:07:40,360
Come check it out!
Authentic export surplus!

152
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:41,270
New store opening!

153
00:07:41,270 --> 00:07:42,400
Buy more, save more!

154
00:07:42,510 --> 00:07:44,240
Ladies, see anything you like?

155
00:07:44,390 --> 00:07:45,240
This is 20 yuan.

156
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:46,360
I'll give you 20% off if you buy it.

157
00:07:46,360 --> 00:07:47,090
How about it?

158
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:48,390
Thirty yuan.

159
00:07:48,430 --> 00:07:49,240
Forty yuan.

160
00:07:49,270 --> 00:07:50,480
Fifty yuan.

161
00:07:50,630 --> 00:07:51,830
Miss, how about taking a dress?

162
00:07:51,830 --> 00:07:52,600
I'll give you 20% off

163
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:53,400
if you take it.

164
00:07:53,600 --> 00:07:54,600
City inspectors!

165
00:07:54,830 --> 00:07:55,430
Hurry, hurry!

166
00:07:55,430 --> 00:07:56,310
City inspectors.

167
00:07:56,310 --> 00:07:57,000
Sorry.

168
00:07:57,190 --> 00:07:58,120
What do we do with the clothes?

169
00:07:58,120 --> 00:07:59,180
Carry them and run!

170
00:07:59,360 --> 00:07:59,870
I...

171
00:08:00,270 --> 00:08:01,920
City inspectors!

172
00:08:01,950 --> 00:08:03,480
Miss, give me five minutes.

173
00:08:03,510 --> 00:08:04,160
Wait for me!

174
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:04,800
Five minutes!

175
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:05,600
I'll be right back,

176
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:06,930
just taking a quick lap!

177
00:08:12,530 --> 00:08:13,160
Stop!

178
00:08:14,190 --> 00:08:14,750
Oh my god!

179
00:08:15,390 --> 00:08:16,310
What a—what a—

180
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:17,680
What a coincidence, Sir.

181
00:08:17,680 --> 00:08:19,040
Not a coincidence at all.

182
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:20,480
I've been waiting here for you.

183
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:21,480
According to Article 18,

184
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:22,830
Paragraph 2
of the Haizhou City Regulations

185
00:08:22,830 --> 00:08:24,430
on Appearance
and Environmental Sanitation...

186
00:08:24,430 --> 00:08:25,040
Captain.

187
00:08:26,480 --> 00:08:27,000
Got her.

188
00:08:27,390 --> 00:08:28,870
No, no, no. Sir.

189
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:30,190
This is my first offense.

190
00:08:30,190 --> 00:08:31,040
First offense, let me go.

191
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:31,500
Please?

192
00:08:31,530 --> 00:08:32,919
What if I catch you again?

193
00:08:32,919 --> 00:08:34,650
I've run into you so many times.

194
00:08:34,669 --> 00:08:35,530
How about this?

195
00:08:35,630 --> 00:08:36,549
I'll run faster next time...

196
00:08:36,549 --> 00:08:37,000
Stop!

197
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:39,549
Stop! You two—follow!

198
00:08:40,480 --> 00:08:41,340
Back alley!

199
00:08:41,750 --> 00:08:42,409
Turn right!

200
00:08:42,870 --> 00:08:43,929
I'm telling you...

201
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:45,440
Don't run!

202
00:08:47,320 --> 00:08:48,270
Stop right there!

203
00:08:48,270 --> 00:08:48,840
Stop!

204
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:51,050
Sir, here's a gift for you.

205
00:08:51,080 --> 00:08:52,960
Wear it, your date will go great!

206
00:09:11,150 --> 00:09:11,840
This kid...

207
00:09:22,990 --> 00:09:24,360
Sir, give me one of these.

208
00:09:24,360 --> 00:09:24,720
Okay.

209
00:09:29,870 --> 00:09:30,480
You've kept this chocolate

210
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:31,630
for a long time.

211
00:09:31,790 --> 00:09:32,600
Don't let it go bad.

212
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:34,060
How about you let me eat it?

213
00:09:34,910 --> 00:09:35,770
It won't go bad.

214
00:09:36,440 --> 00:09:37,460
It'll just melt

215
00:09:37,610 --> 00:09:39,090
into a sticky gooey mess,

216
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:40,580
still tastes good though.

217
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:42,030
Back in high‑school,

218
00:09:42,030 --> 00:09:43,560
Zhi always brought me some.

219
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:44,870
For the longest time

220
00:09:44,870 --> 00:09:45,550
I thought

221
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:47,120
good chocolate

222
00:09:47,150 --> 00:09:49,000
was supposed to turn into sticky goop.

223
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,290
So you prepared this

224
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:51,270
for Qi Zhi?

225
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:56,480
I want to go see him

226
00:09:57,480 --> 00:09:58,540
when I settle down.

227
00:10:08,630 --> 00:10:09,080
Hello?

228
00:10:10,030 --> 00:10:10,550
Hello.

229
00:10:11,150 --> 00:10:12,880
This is Nanqing County Prison.

230
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:14,200
Your visitation request

231
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:15,130
has been denied.

232
00:10:15,270 --> 00:10:16,150
The inmate refuses

233
00:10:16,150 --> 00:10:17,280
to accept visitors.

234
00:10:18,840 --> 00:10:19,510
Why?

235
00:10:21,570 --> 00:10:22,320
The inmate

236
00:10:22,320 --> 00:10:23,960
didn't give a clear explanation.

237
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:24,910
But our principle is

238
00:10:24,910 --> 00:10:26,170
to respect his wishes.

239
00:10:29,670 --> 00:10:31,600
Then can I send him some chocolate?

240
00:10:32,140 --> 00:10:32,750
We provide

241
00:10:32,750 --> 00:10:34,510
all the basic daily necessities here.

242
00:10:34,510 --> 00:10:35,970
We don't accept packages.

243
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:37,750
Alright.

244
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:40,700
Sorry for the trouble. Thank you.

245
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:49,800
You can eat it.

246
00:10:50,240 --> 00:10:51,300
Don't let it go bad.

247
00:10:52,150 --> 00:10:53,480
Not afraid it'll go bad?

248
00:10:53,670 --> 00:10:54,960
Then I won't hold back.

249
00:10:58,080 --> 00:10:59,340
How much is this shirt?

250
00:11:00,030 --> 00:11:01,030
Thirty-five yuan each.

251
00:11:01,030 --> 00:11:01,840
If you buy more,

252
00:11:01,840 --> 00:11:02,620
I can give you a discount.

253
00:11:02,620 --> 00:11:03,220
Let me see.

254
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:05,290
This one.

255
00:11:05,290 --> 00:11:07,150
This one's perfect for this weather.

256
00:11:07,150 --> 00:11:07,630
Can I try it on?

257
00:11:07,630 --> 00:11:08,490
Sure, go ahead.

258
00:11:10,670 --> 00:11:12,270
Ma'am, a newspaper, please.

259
00:11:13,380 --> 00:11:14,440
Still won't see us?

260
00:11:20,430 --> 00:11:20,960
Okay.

261
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:22,570
Thank you.

262
00:11:22,910 --> 00:11:24,170
Sorry for the trouble.

263
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:25,910
Okay, okay.

264
00:11:26,070 --> 00:11:26,820
Okay, bye.

265
00:11:29,790 --> 00:11:30,990
He still won't see us.

266
00:11:31,790 --> 00:11:33,250
If he won't see us, so be it.

267
00:11:33,870 --> 00:11:35,870
I think this kid has made up his mind.

268
00:11:37,150 --> 00:11:38,030
We won't apply

269
00:11:38,790 --> 00:11:39,920
and won't go see him.

270
00:11:43,550 --> 00:11:44,880
Shi also tried to visit,

271
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:47,390
but he turned her away too.

272
00:11:47,390 --> 00:11:48,990
He won't even see his sister?

273
00:11:52,260 --> 00:11:53,490
You know,

274
00:11:54,750 --> 00:11:56,880
these two kids are both so headstrong.

275
00:11:57,630 --> 00:11:58,440
When they were little,

276
00:11:58,440 --> 00:11:59,510
Shi would call me "Mom"

277
00:11:59,510 --> 00:12:01,200
a hundred times a day.

278
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:04,370
Now that she's grown up,
she's flown the coop.

279
00:12:04,490 --> 00:12:05,630
And I, her own mother,

280
00:12:05,630 --> 00:12:06,960
am less than a stranger.

281
00:12:08,360 --> 00:12:09,560
Don't put it that way.

282
00:12:10,790 --> 00:12:12,240
It's a good thing

283
00:12:12,270 --> 00:12:13,600
that kids have their own ideas.

284
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:15,600
It just shows they're considerate,

285
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:17,740
letting us worry less.

286
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:19,200
Worry less?

287
00:12:19,220 --> 00:12:20,150
Which one of them

288
00:12:20,150 --> 00:12:21,720
has ever made us worry less?

289
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:23,920
Which one has ever been easy?

290
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:25,630
No.

291
00:12:26,870 --> 00:12:27,390
I need to get through

292
00:12:27,390 --> 00:12:28,650
to at least one of them.

293
00:12:28,870 --> 00:12:30,200
Aren't you going to Haizhou tomorrow

294
00:12:30,200 --> 00:12:30,860
to stock up?

295
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:33,360
Go visit Qi Shi.

296
00:12:33,670 --> 00:12:34,880
See where she is

297
00:12:34,910 --> 00:12:36,120
and what big company she's in.

298
00:12:36,120 --> 00:12:37,200
I just don't buy it.

299
00:12:37,510 --> 00:12:39,150
See how she's really doing.

300
00:12:39,170 --> 00:12:39,600
If she's struggling,

301
00:12:39,600 --> 00:12:40,600
bring her home.

302
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:42,960
Why don't you come with me?

303
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:44,890
If I go, who's gonna watch the shop?

304
00:12:45,630 --> 00:12:47,030
Besides, stocking up—

305
00:12:47,390 --> 00:12:47,870
isn't that

306
00:12:47,870 --> 00:12:49,120
you men's business?

307
00:12:49,320 --> 00:12:50,720
Don't try to dump it on me.

308
00:12:50,990 --> 00:12:51,510
Okay.

309
00:12:52,510 --> 00:12:53,830
I'll go see our girl,

310
00:12:54,910 --> 00:12:56,770
then I'll let you know she's okay.

311
00:12:58,030 --> 00:12:59,690
The main thing is stocking up.

312
00:12:59,880 --> 00:13:01,300
Okay, fine.

313
00:13:07,510 --> 00:13:08,240
Come on,

314
00:13:09,480 --> 00:13:10,790
check out my newly upgraded gear.

315
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:11,320
How is it?

316
00:13:11,960 --> 00:13:12,750
Buy on the go,

317
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:14,140
carry it with you,

318
00:13:14,140 --> 00:13:15,070
sell it as you go.

319
00:13:16,030 --> 00:13:17,230
Just set up the grill.

320
00:13:20,150 --> 00:13:20,720
Not bad.

321
00:13:20,770 --> 00:13:21,300
Right?

322
00:13:21,470 --> 00:13:22,480
If I were the strict inspector,

323
00:13:22,480 --> 00:13:23,550
I couldn't find a single fault.

324
00:13:23,550 --> 00:13:24,550
I'm just gonna...

325
00:13:24,910 --> 00:13:25,840
make a run for it.

326
00:13:25,910 --> 00:13:27,440
Careful, don't spill that.

327
00:13:27,670 --> 00:13:28,720
Yeah, I gotta...

328
00:13:28,870 --> 00:13:30,070
Plant my feet firmly,

329
00:13:30,790 --> 00:13:31,920
and start grilling.

330
00:13:31,950 --> 00:13:33,610
Hello, how much is this shirt?

331
00:13:33,960 --> 00:13:34,720
Feel free to look.

332
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:35,580
Let me tell you,

333
00:13:35,630 --> 00:13:36,120
in the building next door,

334
00:13:36,120 --> 00:13:37,270
they charge over 100 yuan for this.

335
00:13:37,270 --> 00:13:38,330
Here, it's only 20 yuan.

336
00:13:38,330 --> 00:13:39,930
Alright, I'll keep looking.

337
00:13:45,060 --> 00:13:46,530
[Dad]

338
00:13:46,410 --> 00:13:48,290
Tired from work every day?

339
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:50,750
Get some lamb skewers! Skewers!

340
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:52,530
W‑What's wrong?

341
00:13:52,770 --> 00:13:54,030
Why are you so nervous?

342
00:13:54,270 --> 00:13:55,840
No—no one. It's nothing.

343
00:13:58,470 --> 00:13:58,910
Here.

344
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:00,510
Dad, I'm in a meeting.

345
00:14:00,670 --> 00:14:01,930
I can't talk right now.

346
00:14:03,270 --> 00:14:04,910
Tired from work every day?

347
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:07,120
Get some lamb skewers,
something different.

348
00:14:07,120 --> 00:14:07,650
Sweetie,

349
00:14:07,780 --> 00:14:08,700
I'm in Haizhou.

350
00:14:08,910 --> 00:14:09,870
When do you get off work?

351
00:14:09,870 --> 00:14:11,390
Authentic charcoal-grilled lamb skewers!

352
00:14:11,390 --> 00:14:12,080
Wang,

353
00:14:12,910 --> 00:14:13,640
keep it down.

354
00:14:13,780 --> 00:14:14,480
Okay, okay.

355
00:14:14,550 --> 00:14:15,280
Try a skewer.

356
00:14:15,670 --> 00:14:16,800
Fresh off the grill.

357
00:14:21,200 --> 00:14:21,630
Hello?

358
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:22,900
Hello, Dad.

359
00:14:23,630 --> 00:14:24,840
Why didn't you

360
00:14:24,840 --> 00:14:26,080
tell me you were coming?

361
00:14:26,080 --> 00:14:27,410
I'm in a meeting at work.

362
00:14:28,360 --> 00:14:28,960
It's fine.

363
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:31,080
Your mom misses you,

364
00:14:31,080 --> 00:14:33,010
so she asked me to come check on you.

365
00:14:33,440 --> 00:14:34,750
What time do you get off work?

366
00:14:34,750 --> 00:14:36,240
How about I go wait for you

367
00:14:36,270 --> 00:14:37,330
at your workplace?

368
00:14:37,910 --> 00:14:38,510
No, no, no.

369
00:14:39,150 --> 00:14:40,680
Hello, how is this dress...

370
00:14:41,390 --> 00:14:41,790
No.

371
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:43,370
What's with that attitude?

372
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:44,750
No, Dad.

373
00:14:45,440 --> 00:14:45,970
Dad, Dad.

374
00:14:46,870 --> 00:14:47,900
Our company

375
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:50,870
has super‑strict confidentiality rules.

376
00:14:51,150 --> 00:14:51,630
And...

377
00:14:52,150 --> 00:14:54,200
there's nowhere to sit at the entrance.

378
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:55,480
You'd have no place to hang out.

379
00:14:55,480 --> 00:14:56,340
How about this:

380
00:14:56,390 --> 00:14:57,550
I'm working really late today,

381
00:14:57,550 --> 00:14:58,530
so you go back first.

382
00:14:58,530 --> 00:14:59,790
Next time, let me know before you come,

383
00:14:59,790 --> 00:15:00,710
then I'll

384
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:03,560
go pick you up at the station.

385
00:15:05,390 --> 00:15:05,990
It's fine.

386
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:08,120
I'll do as you say.

387
00:15:09,850 --> 00:15:11,700
Right, right. My boss is calling me.

388
00:15:11,700 --> 00:15:12,580
I gotta go.

389
00:15:36,840 --> 00:15:38,360
I'm coming back to Haizhou for May Day.

390
00:15:38,360 --> 00:15:39,640
Sure, that's great.

391
00:15:39,670 --> 00:15:40,360
Hurry back.

392
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:42,840
Everyone back home is waiting for you.

393
00:15:42,840 --> 00:15:43,870
Then you'd better host us well.

394
00:15:43,870 --> 00:15:44,960
I'm not coming alone.

395
00:15:44,960 --> 00:15:46,030
Not alone?

396
00:15:46,480 --> 00:15:47,910
Does that mean you have a girlfriend?

397
00:15:47,910 --> 00:15:48,910
Good for you, man.

398
00:15:49,600 --> 00:15:50,000
I'm gonna

399
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:50,960
hype this up

400
00:15:50,980 --> 00:15:52,030
in our class group chat later.

401
00:15:52,030 --> 00:15:53,790
The class monitor is returning home
in glory with his family.

402
00:15:53,790 --> 00:15:55,080
It's my school's debate team,

403
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:56,280
an off-campus event.

404
00:15:56,440 --> 00:15:57,200
Five or six people.

405
00:15:57,200 --> 00:15:58,320
Forget five or six,

406
00:15:58,630 --> 00:15:59,760
even ten or twenty,

407
00:15:59,790 --> 00:16:01,240
I can afford to host them.

408
00:16:01,510 --> 00:16:02,710
If it comes down to it,

409
00:16:02,960 --> 00:16:05,160
I'll ask Qi Shi and the others to join us.

410
00:16:07,550 --> 00:16:08,200
Qi Shi?

411
00:16:09,670 --> 00:16:11,270
Did you get in touch with her?

412
00:16:11,480 --> 00:16:12,080
I didn't.

413
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:14,100
But Fatty is in touch with her.

414
00:16:14,550 --> 00:16:15,930
We can take this opportunity

415
00:16:15,930 --> 00:16:17,260
to have a get-together.

416
00:16:17,270 --> 00:16:18,270
Mind if I sit here?

417
00:16:18,910 --> 00:16:19,970
What's that voice?

418
00:16:20,530 --> 00:16:21,440
I think I just heard

419
00:16:21,440 --> 00:16:22,440
a beautiful girl's voice.

420
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:23,080
Bye.

421
00:16:25,630 --> 00:16:26,960
On the phone with a friend?

422
00:16:26,960 --> 00:16:28,420
My high school classmate.

423
00:16:28,550 --> 00:16:29,670
Remember we're going

424
00:16:29,670 --> 00:16:30,480
to Haizhou for May Day?

425
00:16:30,480 --> 00:16:31,510
I was just telling him.

426
00:16:31,510 --> 00:16:32,200
If he's free,

427
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:33,150
we can all hang out.

428
00:16:33,150 --> 00:16:33,550
Sure.

429
00:16:34,360 --> 00:16:36,290
It'd be great to have a local guide.

430
00:16:37,630 --> 00:16:38,630
Does that mean we can meet

431
00:16:38,630 --> 00:16:40,560
that good neighbor you mentioned?

432
00:16:43,360 --> 00:16:43,960
Her...

433
00:16:44,790 --> 00:16:46,990
We haven't been in touch for a long time.

434
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:48,930
I don't even know if I can reach her.

435
00:16:49,240 --> 00:16:51,040
Don't you have her phone number?

436
00:16:52,080 --> 00:16:52,480
No.

437
00:16:53,630 --> 00:16:54,430
What about QQ?

438
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:56,320
I have her QQ.

439
00:16:56,320 --> 00:16:57,580
Then you can reach her.

440
00:16:58,150 --> 00:16:59,810
Just leave her a message on QQ.

441
00:17:01,270 --> 00:17:02,670
She hasn't logged into QQ

442
00:17:04,359 --> 00:17:05,349
in a long time.

443
00:17:12,050 --> 00:17:12,640
Cao Xin,

444
00:17:13,790 --> 00:17:15,790
where there's a will, there's a way.

445
00:17:23,640 --> 00:17:24,440
You're right.

446
00:17:25,640 --> 00:17:27,640
Where there's a will, there's a way.

447
00:17:28,760 --> 00:17:29,550
Let's go to the library

448
00:17:29,550 --> 00:17:30,310
after we eat.

449
00:17:31,730 --> 00:17:32,530
Didn't you say

450
00:17:32,550 --> 00:17:33,950
you needed a study buddy?

451
00:17:34,550 --> 00:17:35,680
Exams are coming up.

452
00:17:35,790 --> 00:17:37,160
Time for some last‑minute cramming.

453
00:17:37,160 --> 00:17:37,510
Okay.

454
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:06,750
Big news.

455
00:18:06,920 --> 00:18:08,440
Class Monitor Cao has a girlfriend.

456
00:18:08,440 --> 00:18:09,970
Check the class group chat.

457
00:18:39,750 --> 00:18:41,080
Stop spreading rumors.

458
00:18:41,110 --> 00:18:42,570
I don't have a girlfriend.

459
00:18:42,690 --> 00:18:43,690
Come on.

460
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:44,800
I swear I heard

461
00:18:44,830 --> 00:18:46,490
a girl having dinner with you.

462
00:19:26,830 --> 00:19:27,640
Nothing left?

463
00:19:27,790 --> 00:19:28,160
Nope.

464
00:19:28,160 --> 00:19:29,220
I'm locking up now.

465
00:19:33,110 --> 00:19:34,160
What is this?

466
00:19:38,110 --> 00:19:39,790
Don't take random unknown stuff.

467
00:19:39,790 --> 00:19:40,530
Toss it out.

468
00:19:41,750 --> 00:19:42,750
Wait, wait, wait.

469
00:19:43,510 --> 00:19:44,920
What is it?

470
00:19:45,510 --> 00:19:47,440
Look at what it says on the package.

471
00:19:47,650 --> 00:19:49,580
Specialty pastries from Beining.

472
00:19:49,990 --> 00:19:51,320
Cao Xin sent these over?

473
00:20:15,680 --> 00:20:16,160
Cao Xin,

474
00:20:17,680 --> 00:20:19,310
Mrs. Huo really loves

475
00:20:19,470 --> 00:20:21,090
those pastries you sent.

476
00:20:21,680 --> 00:20:23,940
She kept saying how delicious they were.

477
00:20:26,240 --> 00:20:27,350
Next time I don't have class,

478
00:20:27,350 --> 00:20:28,350
I'll bring my roommates over

479
00:20:28,350 --> 00:20:29,810
to support your business.

480
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:30,650
Sure.

481
00:20:30,680 --> 00:20:32,010
Your roommates will get

482
00:20:32,150 --> 00:20:33,550
VIP treatment—10 % off.

483
00:20:33,790 --> 00:20:34,790
No, 20% off.

484
00:20:35,420 --> 00:20:36,610
Ask them

485
00:20:36,640 --> 00:20:37,960
what styles they like,

486
00:20:38,090 --> 00:20:38,920
and I'll stock up in advance

487
00:20:38,920 --> 00:20:39,830
so they don't make a wasted trip.

488
00:20:39,830 --> 00:20:41,400
Sure thing, Boss Qi.

489
00:20:41,960 --> 00:20:43,290
How does that saying go?

490
00:20:43,550 --> 00:20:45,120
"Whatever you do, do it well."

491
00:20:45,120 --> 00:20:46,200
You really figured out

492
00:20:46,200 --> 00:20:47,530
the tricks of the trade.

493
00:20:47,640 --> 00:20:48,790
You bet.

494
00:20:49,510 --> 00:20:50,720
I'm gonna be

495
00:20:50,750 --> 00:20:52,810
the Warren Buffett of street stalls.

496
00:20:53,140 --> 00:20:54,080
Still going on

497
00:20:54,110 --> 00:20:56,000
about Buffett after all these years?

498
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:57,400
Can't let go of that dream.

499
00:20:57,400 --> 00:20:57,800
Right.

500
00:20:58,110 --> 00:20:59,840
Cao Xin asked me for your number.

501
00:20:59,840 --> 00:21:01,480
He wanted us all to get together

502
00:21:01,480 --> 00:21:03,740
in Haizhou during the next long holiday.

503
00:21:04,920 --> 00:21:05,720
I'm not going.

504
00:21:06,680 --> 00:21:08,080
Nothing to see him about.

505
00:21:18,350 --> 00:21:19,110
Cao Xin.

506
00:21:19,230 --> 00:21:21,360
Speak of the devil and he shall appear.

507
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:29,420
Why aren't you answering?

508
00:21:32,160 --> 00:21:33,360
What would I even say?

509
00:21:34,790 --> 00:21:37,650
That I'm running a street stall
and don't have time?

510
00:21:39,390 --> 00:21:40,950
That Qi Shi, who used to compete with him

511
00:21:40,950 --> 00:21:42,680
for first place in everything,

512
00:21:44,030 --> 00:21:46,030
has been reduced to a street vendor.

513
00:21:49,350 --> 00:21:51,150
He would laugh his head off at me.

514
00:21:52,830 --> 00:21:54,000
Cao Xin can be

515
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:55,590
quite sharp-tongued sometimes.

516
00:21:55,590 --> 00:21:57,110
I remember you two
drawing an imaginary line

517
00:21:57,110 --> 00:21:58,790
down the middle of your desks
all through school.

518
00:21:58,790 --> 00:21:59,480
You were either competing over grades

519
00:21:59,480 --> 00:22:00,750
or fighting for
the class monitor position.

520
00:22:00,750 --> 00:22:01,910
Our homeroom teacher even said

521
00:22:01,910 --> 00:22:02,880
you two would even argue over

522
00:22:02,880 --> 00:22:04,400
whether an ant was male or female
if one walked past.

523
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:04,920
Yeah.

524
00:22:06,750 --> 00:22:07,440
Back then,

525
00:22:08,790 --> 00:22:10,240
no matter what it was,

526
00:22:10,260 --> 00:22:11,790
I always had the upper hand over him.

527
00:22:11,790 --> 00:22:12,920
It's different now.

528
00:22:13,550 --> 00:22:14,880
The tables have turned.

529
00:22:16,270 --> 00:22:18,070
I can't even hold a candle to him.

530
00:22:21,430 --> 00:22:22,290
I understand.

531
00:22:22,750 --> 00:22:24,190
If I were you,

532
00:22:24,440 --> 00:22:26,170
I'd struggle with that gap too.

533
00:22:28,030 --> 00:22:29,960
You two keep talking about Cao Xin.

534
00:22:30,200 --> 00:22:31,000
Who is Cao Xin?

535
00:22:31,400 --> 00:22:32,030
Your boyfriend?

536
00:22:32,030 --> 00:22:33,270
No, no, no.

537
00:22:34,440 --> 00:22:34,990
Don't...

538
00:22:35,240 --> 00:22:36,720
Don't buy this in the future.

539
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:38,580
It can't even hold the clothes.

540
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:39,750
But someone did come

541
00:22:39,750 --> 00:22:41,410
looking for you this morning.

542
00:22:42,440 --> 00:22:43,640
Must've been Cao Xin.

543
00:22:43,880 --> 00:22:44,790
Was it a tall,

544
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:45,790
thin guy?

545
00:22:47,200 --> 00:22:48,240
City inspectors!

546
00:22:49,700 --> 00:22:50,740
You grab the cart. I'll grab the clothes.

547
00:22:50,740 --> 00:22:51,440
-Hurry up.
-Okay.

548
00:22:51,440 --> 00:22:52,160
See you at the usual spot.

549
00:22:52,160 --> 00:22:52,510
Okay.

550
00:22:54,200 --> 00:22:55,200
Stop right there!

551
00:22:56,320 --> 00:22:56,760
Stop!

552
00:22:56,790 --> 00:22:57,640
Stop! Don't run!

553
00:22:57,640 --> 00:22:58,070
Don't run!

554
00:22:58,070 --> 00:22:58,550
Stop!

555
00:22:59,830 --> 00:23:00,760
Stop! Don't run!

556
00:23:03,320 --> 00:23:03,790
Stop!

557
00:23:03,790 --> 00:23:04,790
Don't move! Stop!

558
00:23:05,750 --> 00:23:06,410
Don't move!

559
00:23:10,030 --> 00:23:11,270
Who? Who is it? Who?

560
00:23:16,060 --> 00:23:17,130
Stop! Don't run!

561
00:23:17,160 --> 00:23:17,550
Stop!

562
00:23:26,350 --> 00:23:26,920
Dad?

563
00:23:27,680 --> 00:23:28,070
Here.

564
00:23:28,510 --> 00:23:29,840
What are you doing here?

565
00:23:31,290 --> 00:23:32,690
Pretty impressive, huh?

566
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:34,610
Who else could it be?

567
00:23:39,240 --> 00:23:39,770
Let's go.

568
00:24:03,240 --> 00:24:03,640
Dad,

569
00:24:04,440 --> 00:24:05,300
give them to me.

570
00:24:11,000 --> 00:24:11,530
Sweetie,

571
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:14,800
why are you living in a basement?

572
00:24:15,620 --> 00:24:17,020
It looks like a doghouse.

573
00:24:18,920 --> 00:24:20,920
It depends on where the doghouse is.

574
00:24:21,030 --> 00:24:22,070
Dad, look.

575
00:24:22,400 --> 00:24:23,110
This is

576
00:24:23,110 --> 00:24:24,410
a downtown basement.

577
00:24:24,440 --> 00:24:25,500
That's different.

578
00:24:25,750 --> 00:24:27,080
I worked hard to rent it.

579
00:24:30,830 --> 00:24:31,690
Is it safe here?

580
00:24:32,960 --> 00:24:33,480
Yes.

581
00:24:35,200 --> 00:24:35,590
Dad,

582
00:24:36,190 --> 00:24:37,110
I'm telling you, this place

583
00:24:37,110 --> 00:24:38,220
is perfect for me.

584
00:24:38,440 --> 00:24:38,880
Look,

585
00:24:39,590 --> 00:24:41,190
there's no direct sunlight.

586
00:24:41,310 --> 00:24:41,830
And

587
00:24:42,110 --> 00:24:43,050
I have a fan.

588
00:24:43,680 --> 00:24:44,830
I don't even need to buy

589
00:24:44,830 --> 00:24:46,030
an air conditioner in summer.

590
00:24:46,030 --> 00:24:46,920
It stays naturally cool.

591
00:24:46,920 --> 00:24:48,040
A fan is enough.

592
00:24:48,070 --> 00:24:48,930
It saves money.

593
00:24:58,070 --> 00:24:58,550
Dad,

594
00:24:59,640 --> 00:25:00,440
I told you

595
00:25:01,830 --> 00:25:02,920
over the phone

596
00:25:03,310 --> 00:25:04,880
that I left a big company

597
00:25:05,400 --> 00:25:06,720
for something better.

598
00:25:07,590 --> 00:25:07,960
I

599
00:25:09,200 --> 00:25:10,160
really do feel like

600
00:25:10,160 --> 00:25:11,550
I got something better.

601
00:25:17,550 --> 00:25:19,010
Stop looking around, Dad.

602
00:25:20,050 --> 00:25:21,710
I'll get you something to eat.

603
00:25:38,200 --> 00:25:38,590
Dad,

604
00:25:38,770 --> 00:25:40,590
the BBQ stand upstairs is pretty good.

605
00:25:40,590 --> 00:25:41,740
Let me treat you.

606
00:25:42,880 --> 00:25:43,340
No need.

607
00:25:44,590 --> 00:25:45,680
Let's just make do.

608
00:25:46,080 --> 00:25:47,610
You have steamed buns here.

609
00:25:48,310 --> 00:25:49,710
With some soybean paste,

610
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:50,730
it's enough.

611
00:25:53,880 --> 00:25:54,270
Here.

612
00:26:08,590 --> 00:26:09,400
Hey, Sweetie,

613
00:26:12,270 --> 00:26:13,670
why does your steamed bun

614
00:26:14,240 --> 00:26:14,750
taste a bit

615
00:26:14,750 --> 00:26:16,950
like spicy and sour shredded potatoes?

616
00:26:17,070 --> 00:26:18,160
Sour?

617
00:26:19,240 --> 00:26:20,370
Could it be spoiled?

618
00:26:20,740 --> 00:26:21,480
Smell it.

619
00:26:22,110 --> 00:26:23,310
Let me taste it again.

620
00:26:26,160 --> 00:26:26,960
No, no,

621
00:26:27,640 --> 00:26:28,640
it's not spoiled.

622
00:26:28,790 --> 00:26:29,390
It's fine.

623
00:26:30,040 --> 00:26:30,880
I've got it.

624
00:26:31,200 --> 00:26:32,200
It tastes a little

625
00:26:33,040 --> 00:26:34,440
like sweet and sour fish.

626
00:26:35,880 --> 00:26:37,280
Great. It's not spoiled.

627
00:26:40,960 --> 00:26:42,400
It really does

628
00:26:42,830 --> 00:26:43,890
have a meaty aroma.

629
00:26:43,920 --> 00:26:45,350
Crispy on the outside,
tender on the inside.

630
00:26:45,350 --> 00:26:46,080
And no bones.

631
00:26:46,590 --> 00:26:47,250
Delicious.

632
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:49,940
Let me try mine.

633
00:26:51,110 --> 00:26:51,750
Let me see.

634
00:26:57,960 --> 00:26:58,890
Spicy crayfish.

635
00:27:00,960 --> 00:27:01,690
Try it again.

636
00:27:04,270 --> 00:27:05,070
It also tastes

637
00:27:06,000 --> 00:27:07,350
a bit like braised pork.

638
00:27:08,160 --> 00:27:08,690
Alright.

639
00:27:08,920 --> 00:27:11,450
We've got fish, meat, and crayfish
all in one.

640
00:27:17,030 --> 00:27:17,560
Sweetie,

641
00:27:20,750 --> 00:27:21,590
even though

642
00:27:22,590 --> 00:27:24,920
you're going through some hard times now,

643
00:27:26,350 --> 00:27:28,030
the taste of life

644
00:27:28,400 --> 00:27:30,960
is just like this steamed bun.

645
00:27:32,610 --> 00:27:36,570
♪ The wind blows my hair apart ♪

646
00:27:33,210 --> 00:27:34,920
If you say it's sweet and sour fish,

647
00:27:34,920 --> 00:27:36,350
then it's sweet and sour fish.

648
00:27:36,350 --> 00:27:37,680
If you say it's spicy crayfish,

649
00:27:37,680 --> 00:27:39,140
then it's spicy crayfish.

650
00:27:39,260 --> 00:27:42,940
♪ The story slowly gets complicated too ♪

651
00:27:39,550 --> 00:27:40,200
So,

652
00:27:42,070 --> 00:27:43,670
how you want to live your life

653
00:27:45,480 --> 00:27:46,720
is entirely up to you.

654
00:27:45,920 --> 00:27:50,930
♪ We never became anyone's myth ♪

655
00:27:47,510 --> 00:27:47,920
Right?

656
00:27:51,850 --> 00:27:56,930
♪ Only learned to grow up in the rain ♪

657
00:27:55,200 --> 00:27:55,750
Sweetie,

658
00:27:58,070 --> 00:27:59,590
I know you're feeling wronged.

659
00:27:59,590 --> 00:28:03,180
♪ Should we blame fate? ♪

660
00:28:02,350 --> 00:28:03,750
You used to be number one,

661
00:28:04,960 --> 00:28:05,640
and now

662
00:28:05,680 --> 00:28:09,730
♪ Adulthood is bandaging your own falls ♪

663
00:28:06,440 --> 00:28:08,300
you're setting up a street stall.

664
00:28:10,310 --> 00:28:12,350
It doesn't sound good when people ask.

665
00:28:12,350 --> 00:28:15,380
♪ Rented room, last bus ♪

666
00:28:15,410 --> 00:28:17,640
♪ Where's the future? ♪

667
00:28:18,260 --> 00:28:22,930
♪ How long since I dared
to say I'm scared ♪

668
00:28:18,640 --> 00:28:19,440
But it's okay.

669
00:28:20,720 --> 00:28:21,850
It's okay, sweetie.

670
00:28:22,750 --> 00:28:23,680
I believe in you.

671
00:28:26,030 --> 00:28:26,830
Who are you?

672
00:28:26,410 --> 00:28:29,790
♪ We have nothing,
yet still we rush about ♪

673
00:28:27,310 --> 00:28:29,550
You're my daughter, Qi Aihua's kid,

674
00:28:30,400 --> 00:28:30,880
right?

675
00:28:32,150 --> 00:28:32,960
There are no cowards

676
00:28:32,500 --> 00:28:36,800
♪ Because you're here, there's an answer ♪

677
00:28:33,400 --> 00:28:34,330
in our Qi family.

678
00:28:34,680 --> 00:28:35,280
It's okay.

679
00:28:38,880 --> 00:28:40,980
♪ Past dreams covered in dust ♪

680
00:28:39,880 --> 00:28:40,480
Besides,

681
00:28:41,010 --> 00:28:43,470
♪ It doesn't matter ♪

682
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:44,330
don't look down on running a street stall.

683
00:28:44,400 --> 00:28:45,600
What's wrong with it?

684
00:28:45,900 --> 00:28:51,950
♪ Some things just have to
be this way for now ♪

685
00:28:47,000 --> 00:28:48,130
You running a stall—

686
00:28:49,270 --> 00:28:51,160
that's following
in your old man's footsteps.

687
00:28:51,160 --> 00:28:51,690
You know?

688
00:28:54,160 --> 00:28:55,020
Let me tell you,

689
00:28:55,640 --> 00:28:58,200
back when I got laid off,

690
00:28:59,270 --> 00:29:00,470
I thought it was over.

691
00:29:00,670 --> 00:29:01,800
The sky was falling.

692
00:29:03,270 --> 00:29:04,130
But guess what?

693
00:29:04,540 --> 00:29:06,110
I supported our whole family

694
00:29:06,110 --> 00:29:07,720
by running a street stall.

695
00:29:09,510 --> 00:29:10,880
Plenty of big shots

696
00:29:11,030 --> 00:29:12,830
started out with street stalls.

697
00:29:14,110 --> 00:29:14,880
Like who?

698
00:29:15,310 --> 00:29:17,000
That customer of mine—Mr. Chen.

699
00:29:17,000 --> 00:29:18,060
Mr. Chen. You know?

700
00:29:18,960 --> 00:29:19,510
Mr. Chen.

701
00:29:20,990 --> 00:29:22,300
Do you know what he used to do?

702
00:29:21,300 --> 00:29:25,550
♪ The world spins too fast,
who hasn't panicked? ♪

703
00:29:23,030 --> 00:29:23,510
No.

704
00:29:23,920 --> 00:29:26,120
He rode a tricycle to sell tofu pudding.

705
00:29:27,980 --> 00:29:34,050
♪ All I see is your gaze ♪

706
00:29:34,710 --> 00:29:39,300
♪ If tomorrow there's nothing left ♪

707
00:29:41,050 --> 00:29:51,040
♪ I'll still walk you home ♪

708
00:29:51,070 --> 00:29:51,800
You're back.

709
00:29:54,480 --> 00:29:55,010
Alright.

710
00:29:56,160 --> 00:29:57,260
Now that I've seen you,

711
00:29:57,260 --> 00:29:58,500
I can rest easy.

712
00:30:01,160 --> 00:30:02,240
Your mom—

713
00:30:03,880 --> 00:30:05,590
after all these years, you know her.

714
00:30:05,590 --> 00:30:07,050
Sharp tongue, soft heart.

715
00:30:07,920 --> 00:30:09,030
But deep down,

716
00:30:09,440 --> 00:30:11,570
she's always been thinking about you.

717
00:30:14,240 --> 00:30:14,680
Dad,

718
00:30:16,480 --> 00:30:18,550
about me running the street stall—

719
00:30:18,840 --> 00:30:19,720
can you help me

720
00:30:19,750 --> 00:30:21,080
keep it from Mom for now?

721
00:30:21,440 --> 00:30:21,960
What?

722
00:30:23,200 --> 00:30:24,660
Afraid she won't approve?

723
00:30:26,350 --> 00:30:28,750
When has she ever approved
of anything I do?

724
00:30:29,310 --> 00:30:30,350
It's just that

725
00:30:31,440 --> 00:30:33,270
I haven't made anything of myself yet.

726
00:30:33,270 --> 00:30:34,730
I can't face her like this.

727
00:30:34,960 --> 00:30:35,510
Sweetie,

728
00:30:36,270 --> 00:30:37,270
she's your mom.

729
00:30:38,270 --> 00:30:40,160
It's exactly because she's my mom

730
00:30:41,440 --> 00:30:42,570
that I don't want her

731
00:30:43,270 --> 00:30:44,830
to see me like this.

732
00:30:46,590 --> 00:30:48,400
From the day I left home,

733
00:30:48,400 --> 00:30:49,350
I swore

734
00:30:49,960 --> 00:30:51,550
that the next time I see you guys,

735
00:30:51,550 --> 00:30:53,160
I'd be decent

736
00:30:53,480 --> 00:30:54,410
and successful.

737
00:30:56,830 --> 00:30:57,240
Okay,

738
00:30:58,550 --> 00:30:59,950
I respect your decision.

739
00:31:00,440 --> 00:31:02,270
But you have to promise me something.

740
00:31:02,270 --> 00:31:03,270
From now on, whatever comes up,

741
00:31:03,270 --> 00:31:04,960
don't always grit your teeth
and bear it alone,

742
00:31:04,960 --> 00:31:05,510
okay?

743
00:31:06,400 --> 00:31:07,480
In our family,

744
00:31:07,720 --> 00:31:09,270
I will always have your back,

745
00:31:09,270 --> 00:31:09,830
got it?

746
00:31:10,960 --> 00:31:12,310
Alright, hurry back now.

747
00:31:12,310 --> 00:31:13,840
I'll come see you when I can.

748
00:31:49,720 --> 00:31:50,640
Yeah, right here.

749
00:31:50,640 --> 00:31:51,370
How is it?

750
00:31:51,480 --> 00:31:52,840
Our botanical garden in Haizhou

751
00:31:52,840 --> 00:31:53,440
is beautiful, isn't it?

752
00:31:53,440 --> 00:31:54,240
It's beautiful.

753
00:31:54,240 --> 00:31:54,810
Really beautiful.

754
00:31:54,810 --> 00:31:55,830
The flowers are pretty too.

755
00:31:55,830 --> 00:31:57,030
The flowers blooming
over there are so pretty.

756
00:31:57,030 --> 00:31:58,270
To the left is Wild Duck Lake.

757
00:31:58,270 --> 00:31:59,030
Up ahead there are a few

758
00:31:59,030 --> 00:32:00,200
landmark buildings.

759
00:32:00,200 --> 00:32:01,270
They're all free to visit,

760
00:32:01,270 --> 00:32:02,800
so you can go check them out.

761
00:32:03,240 --> 00:32:04,680
Which one do you want to hit first?

762
00:32:04,680 --> 00:32:05,270
Wild Duck Lake.

763
00:32:05,270 --> 00:32:06,110
Let's go to Wild Duck Lake first.

764
00:32:06,110 --> 00:32:07,840
Alright, off to Wild Duck Lake.

765
00:32:10,000 --> 00:32:11,060
What are you doing?

766
00:32:12,510 --> 00:32:12,840
What?

767
00:32:13,510 --> 00:32:15,310
I called Qi Shi, but she didn't answer.

768
00:32:15,310 --> 00:32:16,370
You give her a call.

769
00:32:16,740 --> 00:32:17,480
What's the rush?

770
00:32:17,480 --> 00:32:18,370
Call her later.

771
00:32:18,510 --> 00:32:19,270
Hurry up.

772
00:32:22,400 --> 00:32:23,340
Okay, okay, okay.

773
00:32:23,340 --> 00:32:24,540
I'll call, I'll call.

774
00:32:25,200 --> 00:32:27,160
But let's be clear—I'm only calling once.

775
00:32:27,160 --> 00:32:28,480
I don't care if she answers or not.

776
00:32:28,480 --> 00:32:31,610
She didn't answer you.
You really think she'd answer me?

777
00:32:39,750 --> 00:32:40,200
Hello?

778
00:32:40,220 --> 00:32:41,090
She answered.

779
00:32:41,440 --> 00:32:42,440
What should I say?

780
00:32:43,310 --> 00:32:44,400
Um, Qi Shi...

781
00:32:44,590 --> 00:32:45,270
Tianji?

782
00:32:47,030 --> 00:32:48,030
What are you up to?

783
00:32:48,510 --> 00:32:50,330
I'm in Haizhou.

784
00:32:51,000 --> 00:32:52,000
Are you busy?

785
00:32:52,920 --> 00:32:54,070
Let's get together.

786
00:32:55,550 --> 00:32:57,160
I'm quite busy. I don't have time.

787
00:32:57,160 --> 00:32:57,790
Cao Xin,

788
00:32:58,480 --> 00:33:00,010
aren't you guys going over?

789
00:33:01,790 --> 00:33:02,590
Wait a moment.

790
00:33:04,000 --> 00:33:04,660
She hung up.

791
00:33:05,200 --> 00:33:06,550
Shoot, you got found out.

792
00:33:06,550 --> 00:33:07,680
She heard your name.

793
00:33:09,070 --> 00:33:09,510
Well.

794
00:33:09,870 --> 00:33:12,070
Let's go check out Wild Duck Lake first.

795
00:33:12,790 --> 00:33:13,160
What?

796
00:33:13,720 --> 00:33:14,780
Nothing, nothing.

797
00:33:17,790 --> 00:33:18,920
She's calling back.

798
00:33:19,920 --> 00:33:21,200
Hello, Qi Shi.

799
00:33:21,400 --> 00:33:22,550
Hello, Tianji.

800
00:33:22,830 --> 00:33:24,350
I missed you so much.

801
00:33:24,350 --> 00:33:25,610
I really want to hang out with you,

802
00:33:25,610 --> 00:33:26,810
just the two of us.

803
00:33:27,200 --> 00:33:28,240
Too bad I'm so busy,

804
00:33:28,240 --> 00:33:28,790
no time.

805
00:33:29,050 --> 00:33:30,130
I'm working

806
00:33:30,160 --> 00:33:31,850
at a Fortune 500 company here.

807
00:33:31,950 --> 00:33:32,970
Because of my outstanding performance,

808
00:33:32,970 --> 00:33:33,960
my boss handpicked me

809
00:33:33,960 --> 00:33:35,550
for a business trip to the US.

810
00:33:35,550 --> 00:33:36,960
There's a whole Pacific Ocean

811
00:33:36,960 --> 00:33:39,070
between us right now.

812
00:33:39,480 --> 00:33:40,440
You wouldn't even see me

813
00:33:40,440 --> 00:33:41,440
if I waved at you.

814
00:33:41,460 --> 00:33:43,440
Working hard every day?

815
00:33:43,640 --> 00:33:45,640
Have some lamb skewers to recharge!

816
00:33:45,740 --> 00:33:46,880
Tired from work every day?

817
00:33:46,880 --> 00:33:48,440
Come try some lamb skewers!

818
00:33:48,680 --> 00:33:50,030
I'm going into a meeting.

819
00:33:50,030 --> 00:33:50,590
Um,

820
00:33:50,880 --> 00:33:51,940
I'm busy, gotta go.

821
00:33:52,440 --> 00:33:53,240
Hello? Hello?

822
00:33:56,350 --> 00:33:57,440
Lamb skewers?

823
00:33:58,480 --> 00:34:00,410
Do Americans eat lamb skewers too?

824
00:34:01,400 --> 00:34:02,160
Chinatown.

825
00:34:02,520 --> 00:34:03,800
I don't know

826
00:34:03,830 --> 00:34:05,410
if Americans eat lamb skewers,

827
00:34:05,410 --> 00:34:06,070
but I suddenly

828
00:34:06,070 --> 00:34:07,600
really want some right now.

829
00:34:09,030 --> 00:34:09,889
I'm hungry too.

830
00:34:10,150 --> 00:34:10,630
Where in Haizhou

831
00:34:10,630 --> 00:34:12,000
has the best lamb skewers?

832
00:34:12,000 --> 00:34:13,360
You should've said so earlier.

833
00:34:13,360 --> 00:34:14,820
I'll take you to Haizhou's

834
00:34:14,880 --> 00:34:15,880
biggest night market.

835
00:34:15,880 --> 00:34:18,080
Let's go check out Wild Duck Lake first.

836
00:34:19,150 --> 00:34:20,210
The air is so fresh.

837
00:34:25,630 --> 00:34:26,250
I'm telling you,

838
00:34:26,250 --> 00:34:27,840
I've been watching for days.

839
00:34:27,840 --> 00:34:29,699
Because my accounts don't add up.

840
00:34:30,840 --> 00:34:32,190
Either rolls of paper towels go missing,

841
00:34:32,190 --> 00:34:33,790
or a few bottles of hand soap.

842
00:34:34,280 --> 00:34:35,600
Stuff like bean paste

843
00:34:35,630 --> 00:34:38,090
and salted duck eggs
disappear even faster.

844
00:34:38,360 --> 00:34:39,670
One day takes the cake.

845
00:34:39,929 --> 00:34:40,710
I had leftover fried dough sticks

846
00:34:40,710 --> 00:34:42,070
and vegetable turnovers

847
00:34:42,070 --> 00:34:43,000
in the morning,

848
00:34:43,150 --> 00:34:44,949
planning to eat them for dinner.

849
00:34:45,760 --> 00:34:46,360
But

850
00:34:46,880 --> 00:34:48,880
the thief stole every last bit of it.

851
00:34:49,830 --> 00:34:50,370
I mean,

852
00:34:50,400 --> 00:34:51,800
it's not like they were stealing
anything expensive,

853
00:34:51,800 --> 00:34:53,260
but it's just so annoying.

854
00:34:54,150 --> 00:34:56,750
That thief really knows how to live
on a budget.

855
00:35:25,260 --> 00:35:26,670
Honey, honey, it's me.

856
00:35:28,440 --> 00:35:28,880
Me.

857
00:35:31,230 --> 00:35:32,760
What the hell are you doing?

858
00:35:46,710 --> 00:35:48,760
Well, the place was

859
00:35:48,840 --> 00:35:49,510
such a mess,

860
00:35:49,670 --> 00:35:51,070
so I tidied it up a little.

861
00:35:51,280 --> 00:35:52,210
These things...

862
00:35:54,000 --> 00:35:54,550
Qi Aihua,

863
00:35:54,550 --> 00:35:56,210
are you seeing another woman?

864
00:35:57,000 --> 00:35:57,670
Who? Me?

865
00:35:58,190 --> 00:35:58,840
No.

866
00:35:59,200 --> 00:35:59,960
Tell me the truth.

867
00:35:59,960 --> 00:36:01,290
Are you seeing someone?

868
00:36:01,400 --> 00:36:02,800
Don't accuse me wrongly.

869
00:36:03,240 --> 00:36:04,110
How could that be?

870
00:36:04,110 --> 00:36:04,840
Then who are

871
00:36:04,840 --> 00:36:06,040
all these things for?

872
00:36:06,550 --> 00:36:07,000
No,

873
00:36:07,000 --> 00:36:08,190
nothing like that, I...

874
00:36:08,190 --> 00:36:09,160
Qi Aihua,

875
